What do we need to do in preparation for the fumigation service?

To ensure a safe and effective treatment, please complete these steps before our team arrives:
- •  Cover or Store Food Items: Seal or store all open foodstuffs to prevent contamination.
- •  Remove Pets and Children: Keep pets and children out of the treated area during service.
- •  Protect Tropical Fish: Cover fish tanks with a damp cloth and turn off air pumps.
- •  Open Cupboards and Drawers: Leave cupboard drawers and doors open for full access.
- •  Clear Clutter: Remove items from floors and surfaces to allow thorough treatment.
- •  Notify Us of Concerns: Inform us of any allergies, sensitivities, or specific areas needing attention.

What do we do after the fumigation service?

To ensure the best results and keep your space safe and comfortable, please follow these simple steps after your pest control treatment:

After Your Treatment:
- •  Open windows and doors to let fresh air circulate before returning indoors.
- •  Wash all cooking and eating utensils thoroughly before using them again.
- •  Leave treated surfaces untouched. Allow the treatment to dry completely for maximum effectiveness.
- •  Wait until the treatment has dried before putting items back in place.
- •  Avoid disturbing gel baits placed behind or inside appliances, as they’re working to eliminate pests.

